    "theorem": "HildebrandBoxAsymptoticAudit.corrected_box_asymptotic_certificate",
    "statement": "theorem corrected_box_asymptotic_certificate : (∀ d : ℕ, Tendsto (fun n : ℕ => ((n-1).descFactorial d : ℝ)/(n : ℝ)^d) atTop (𝓝 1)) ∧ (∀ (d : ℕ), 2 ≤ d → ∀ (ε : ℝ), 0<ε → Tendsto (sourceWidth d ε) atTop atTop ∧ (∀ n : ℕ, (sourceWidth d ε n)^d=sourceCoefficient d ε*(n : ℝ)^(d-1)) ∧ Tendsto (correctionFactor d ε) atTop (𝓝 1)) ∧ (∀ (d : ℕ) (ε : ℝ) (p : ℕ) (m : Fin d → ℤ) (i : Fin d), cellLower d ε p m i=(m i : ℝ)*(ε/2)^(1/(d : ℝ))* (p : ℝ)^(((d : ℝ)-1)/(d : ℝ))/(2*(p : ℝ)) ∧ cellUpper d ε p m i=((m i : ℝ)+1)*(ε/2)^(1/(d : ℝ))* (p : ℝ)^(((d : ℝ)-1)/(d : ℝ))/(2*(p : ℝ))) ∧ (∀ (p d : ℕ) [Fact p.Prime] (a₀ : ZMod p) (h : d ≤ p-1), Fintype.card (FullSupports p d a₀)=(p-1).descFactorial d ∧ sourceLaw p d a₀ h=@uniformLaw (FullSupports p d a₀) inferInstance (full_support_nonempty a₀ h)) ∧ (∀ (d : ℕ), 2 ≤ d → ∀ (ε : ℝ), 0<ε → ∃ N : ℕ, ∃ hN : d+1 ≤ N, ∀ (p : ℕ) [Fact p.Prime] (hp : N ≤ p) (a₀ j : ZMod p), j ≠ 0 → ∀ m : Fin d → ℤ, sourceProbability p d a₀ j (dimension_fits hN hp) (cellLower d ε p m) (cellUpper d ε p m) ≤ 1.1*(ε/2)/((2 : ℝ)^d*(p : ℝ))) ∧ (∀ ε : ℝ, (∀ n : ℕ, sourceWidth 1 ε n=ε/4) ∧ ¬ Tendsto (sourceWidth 1 ε) atTop atTop) ∧ (∀ (p : ℕ) [Fact p.Prime], 3 ≤ p → cellProbability p=1/((p-1 : ℕ) : ℝ) ∧ ¬ cellProbability p ≤ printedBound p) ∧ (¬ ∃ N : ℕ, ∀ (p : ℕ) [Fact p.Prime], N ≤ p → 3 ≤ p → cellProbability p ≤ printedBound p)",
    "decl_sha256": "ac4b0f9ca0aed6dcff2ab1d2c9f94db4b35439e81fd4401d449e0a85e544ce54",
    "scope": "Corrected Hildebrand author-preprint Lemma2, k=d+1>=3: for every fixed d>=2 and epsilon>0 there exists a threshold independent of integer cell shifts, fixed first support point and nonzero Fourier index, such that for every sufficiently large prime the actual full-conditional uniform support-box probability is <=literal1.1*(epsilon/2)/(2^d*p). Literal real-power endpoints are bound. Actual support cardinality and source uniform-law equality are derived. Actual descending-factorial normalization tends1, source integer-coordinate width tends infinity with exact dth-power identity, and the resulting correction factor tends1; no asymptotic/probability/mixing premise supplied. For k2 the source width is exactly epsilon/4 and does not tend to infinity. The preceding actual acknowledged k2 singleton probability/no-eventual-prime-bound counter is included. Standard foundations/default limits; no holes/custom axioms/native evaluation/raised limits/global flags/waivers/native experiment/paid compute/upload. This proves corrected counting, preserves the qualified mixing theorems and leaves the stronger expected random-support mixing exponent open. No novelty claim.",
